<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Evander Q1 pre-capex net profit up.</title>
<headline>Evander Q1 pre-capex net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending  41.58 vs 34.99</p>
<p>    Capital spending			   8.76 vs 15.5</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			  4,930 vs 4,792</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled/treated		 874,000 vs 850,000</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)				5.6 vs 5.6</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			   43,219 vs 49,339</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)			50,983 vs 55,922</p>
<p>Full name: Evander Gold Mines Ltd, managed by Gengold Ltd  </p>
<p>Kinross Division:</p>
<p>    Capital spending			 3.86  vs 9.1</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			 2,520 vs 2,375</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled			  426,000 vs 405,000</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)			     5.9 vs 5.9</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			  43,219 vs 46,464</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)		     51,052 vs 55,805</p>
<p>Leslie Division:</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  0.47 vs 1.71</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			  670  vs 656</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled			  119,000 vs 118,000</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)			     5.6 vs 5.6</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			  45,658 vs 46,966</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)		     52,359 vs 56,007</p>
<p>Winkelhaak Division:</p>
<p>    Capital spending			 4,435 vs 4,689</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			 1,740 vs 1,761</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled			  329,000 vs 327,000</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)			     5.3 vs 5.4</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			  51,954 vs 54,100</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)		     50,719 vs 56,049</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the mineral rights -- containing an estimated 1.7 million ounces of gold -- acquired by the company in a recent exchange with Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd will be purchased by the company for 25.2 million rand to be settled by an issue of the company's shares.</p>
<p>Evander said it treated 62,000 tonnes (December 1996: 15,000) of surface material at a yield of 0.8 g/t.</p>
<p>The balance of the ore milled of 812,000 (December 1996: 835,000) tonnes was sourced from underground and yielded 6.01 (December 1996: 5.73) g/t.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
